# Checkbox

A native checkbox with its label, for yes/no choices applied when the
form is submitted. Basecoat styles it with the `input` class; wrapping
both in a `label` makes the whole row the click target with no
`for`/`id` wiring.

<%= embed :checkbox, :default %>

```html
<label class="label gap-3">
  <input type="checkbox" class="input" name="consent">
  Accept terms and conditions
</label>

<label class="label gap-3">
  <input type="checkbox" class="input" name="include_discharged" checked>
  Include discharged patients
</label>

<label class="label gap-3">
  <input type="checkbox" class="input" disabled>
  Unavailable option
</label>
```

## When to use

- A binary choice inside a form: consent, "include discharged",
  feature opt-in.
- Several independent picks from a list — one checkbox per option.

## When not to use

- Immediate on/off outside a submit flow — use `switch`.
- Mutually exclusive options — use `radio_group`.
- Confirming a destructive action — that is a `dialog`, not a
  "tick to confirm" checkbox.

## Anatomy and options

One native input plus its label. `class="input"` does the styling;
everything else is the platform's checkbox API:

- `name` / `value` — what the form submits when ticked.
- `checked`, `disabled`, `required` — native attributes, no wiring.
- Wrap input and text in `label.label gap-3` as above. Only reach for
  a separate `<label for=…>` when the two cannot nest in the layout.

## Do and don't

- Do phrase the label as the positive state being enabled: "Include
  discharged patients" — ticking means yes.
- Don't use negative labels ("Don't send notifications") — a ticked
  negative is a double negative.
- Don't default-tick consent or anything with consequences the user
  hasn't seen.
- Do keep checkbox groups under roughly seven options; longer lists
  want search (`combobox`) or a different model.

## Accessibility and content

- Native `input[type=checkbox]` inside its label: clicking anywhere in
  the label toggles, Space toggles, state is announced — nothing to
  add.
- An unticked `required` checkbox blocks submission natively.
- Label is sentence case, no terminal punctuation.
